 ### Done
 - **Creator CR4 batch A3, spooky (2026-11-13; docs/CREATOR.md "CR4 batch A3"):** 60 new parts live: 10 horns (gene `horns` 16..25), 16 tails (`tail` 16..31), 14 wings (`wings` 10..23), 4 halos (`halo` 12..15) and 16 auras (`aura` 8..23), hand-written part scripts in `core/data/parts/spooky` (no new painter code), shape gate, cost weights, frozen ids, review line A3, contact sheets incl. the new `portrait_sheet --slot tail|wings --views` (figure and the fighter's five views), runner walk-through `creator_parts_spooky.txt`, `test_cr4_a3.c`. Old saves, premades and Classic islands unchanged. Not in A3 (deep fields, need CR5): horn page 2 (6), horn / antenna bits (32), tail accessories (16), wing accessories (8), halo page 2 (6) = 68 of the batch's 134 (the other 6 are the painted halos live since CR3).
+- **LV7a, level art kit part 1 (2026-11-13, LEVELS round 2; `docs/LEVELS.md` "LV7a", plan 8.6):** 7 shared textures (ids 48..54: steam tile, pipe steel, office carpet, cubicle fabric, felt, ledger page, vault metal) and 3 skies (OVERCAST, INK, DUSK_LANTERNS) as generated data in `core/gen/art_data.c`; ids 56..63 stay the level slots. `TEX_COUNT` / `SKY_COUNT` stay the old counts on the PS1 (the new frames sit behind `#ifndef DOOMO_PLATFORM_PS1`, `packart.py` stops there: PS1 EXE unchanged); GBA RAM net negative (the overworld frame flag array is gone); ROM growth listed in the status file. Left for LV7b: 4 demon sprite sets, Duchess portrait, usable / prop / collectible banks, 6 songs, ~12 SFX (the SFX budget has only 1,359 B of headroom: needs an owner decision).
 - **Levels LV0 (2026-11-13, level registry and records; `docs/LEVELS.md` "LV0", plan section 9):** `LV_COUNT` 31 (the seven built levels, Hell Breach 8-16 as ids 7..15, the 15 Arrears Notices as 16..30), the table moved to `levels2.c` with a registry (page, platform manifest, dark flag, unlock rule and its locked reason; rules by level, chapter, episode, flag, New Game+), the 24 new levels registered as not built (no map: not shown, never startable), the `BRCH` save chunk (slot 14, 148 B for all 24 levels and the arc state, 80 B on the GBA which lists 7 of them, declared 160 B; round trip, empty / absent / bad chunk, a save from another platform loads), the level select in pages (UP / DOWN, pips per page, 15 fit at 240 wide; one page today and pixel-identical to before: 2,196 runner screenshots byte-identical to the base). GBA: EWRAM 15,444 -> 15,460 B free (on `0df72845`, after CR3), IWRAM unchanged; PS1: -144 B resident, the EXE ends at 0x801ef450 against the base's 0x801ef4e0, 68,512 B below the stack top against 68,368 B (the PS1 build keeps the old seven until its LEVELS share is released); `make -C core test` 1,133 passed, SAN, check-gen, xcheck, `make -C gba test`, `dc-host-test`, `make -C dc`, PS1 build + game_smoke + the level-select harness script PASS. Next: LV1, LV10, then the level packages.
 - **LV10, level test harness (2026-11-13, `docs/LEVELS.md` "Level test harness"):** `tools/breach_scripts.py` (a `gen` generator) writes the runner, GBA, PS1 and Dreamcast scripts of every level from one list (the 7 existing levels first); `make -C gba test-breach2` plays the 7 on the GBA harness (autopilot, three fps windows, `vhash-seq` printed (equal across two manual runs, not gated), floors at 85% of the first measurement); `tools/breach_fps.py` builds the platform x level x window fps table; `core/tests/test_levels2.c` asserts the autopilot finishes every level at Plushie in Hell Breach and Time Trial mode and sweeps the whole mode x difficulty matrix on request. The GBA autopilot runs at 4-17 drawn fps (combat, the speed stream's). PS1 / Dreamcast scripts generated and syntax-checked, not run (toolchains were still installing). Partial: the autopilot finishes 44 of 84 mode x difficulty cells (14 asserted); the rest is LV6's. Core 1135 passed (SAN=1 the same, the 4 known UBSan reports), GBA tests and `test-breach2` (floors on) green, no resident byte on any platform.
 - **Creator CR4 batch A2, hair (2026-11-13; docs/CREATOR.md "CR4 batch A2", GBA ledger row 45):** 40 new parts live: 32 hair styles (gene `hair_style` 32..63) and 8 beards (`facial_hair` 8..15), hand-written part scripts (`core/data/parts/hair`, `beard`), shape gate, cost weights, frozen ids, review line A2, contact sheets incl. the new `portrait_sheet --interplay` (hats x big hair, buns, horns), runner walk-through `creator_parts_hair.txt`, `test_cr4_a2.c`. Old saves, premades and Classic islands unchanged. GBA: EWRAM / IWRAM net zero, ROM +20,140 B; PS1: `_end` unchanged (68,368 B below the stack top). Not in A2 (needs CR5 saved deep parts and new `DF_` ids with painter hooks): hair page 2 (24), bangs (12), ahoge (12), hair accessories (52), facial hair page 2 (8) = 108 of the batch's 148.
